{{HEADER}}
<main id="research-lab" tabindex="-1">
<section class="research-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
<div class="orb-backdrop" aria-hidden="true"><img src="assets/kep/cyberalchemy-orb-frozen.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="384" height="384" fetchpriority="high"></div>
<div class="page-width hero-inner">
<p class="eyebrow"><span class="research-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> A research lab</p>
<h1 id="hero-title">Turning intention<br>into systems<br><em>we can understand.</em></h1>
<p class="hero-deck">We explore intelligence, complex systems and how people and machines work together.</p>
<p class="hero-support">Through cybernetics, scientific inquiry and software, we work to turn intentions into understandable, governable systems—even when the AI within them is imperfect and probabilistic.</p>
<div class="hero-actions"><a class="ds-button" href="#research">Explore our research <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="text-link" href="company-brain.html">Meet CyberAlchemy Lab <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
<div class="hero-baseline"><span>Intelligence / Knowledge / Human–machine systems</span><a href="#why">Why CyberAlchemy <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
</div></section>

<section id="why" class="page-width research-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="why-title">
<p class="section-marker">01 / The name</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="why-title">From lead to gold.</h2>
<div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">Alchemy gave us an image: transforming what we have into something we have yet to understand how to make.</p>
<p>Our starting material is an intention—something we want to understand, change or create. We work to turn it into knowledge, models and systems that others can examine and use.</p>
<p><a href="https://asc-cybernetics.org/the-field-of-cybernetics/">Cybernetics</a> gives us a way to study that transformation: observe what happens, compare it with what was intended, respond to the difference and revise our understanding.</p>
<p>The name brings that possibility and responsibility together. We want to transform things. We want to understand what we are transforming.</p></div>
<figure class="research-loop"><div class="loop-steps"><span><small>Ask</small>Intention</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span><small>Express</small>Model</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span><small>Investigate</small>Experiment</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span><small>Examine</small>Evidence</span></div><div class="loop-return"><span aria-hidden="true">↶</span> Evidence changes the next question.</div><figcaption>How we approach inquiry. Each pass can change the model, the experiment or the intention itself.</figcaption></figure>
</div></section>

<section id="culture" class="culture-section" aria-labelledby="culture-title"><div class="page-width section-grid">
<p class="section-marker">02 / Our culture</p>
<div class="section-content"><p class="eyebrow">Two incessant questions</p><h2 id="culture-title" class="culture-questions"><span>What if?</span><span>How to?</span></h2>
<div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">We are a band of deviants and renegades. Curiosity leads us into subjects we do not yet understand.</p><p>We begin by learning. We make our assumptions visible and put our ideas against evidence and criticism. Finding ourselves wrong is part of the work. What matters is whether we notice, understand why and change our course.</p></div>
<dl class="culture-practices"><div><dt>Enter the unfamiliar.</dt><dd>Read, ask, experiment. Expertise is something we work toward.</dd></div><div><dt>Examine the premises.</dt><dd>Use epistemology to question what we know, how we know it and what would change our minds.</dd></div><div><dt>Welcome correction.</dt><dd>Apply the scientific method. Keep counterexamples and failed experiments available for scrutiny.</dd></div><div><dt>Care about the human effort.</dt><dd>Study what people need to understand, review, correct and recover machine work.</dd></div></dl>
</div></div></section>

<section id="research" class="page-width research-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="research-title">
<p class="section-marker">03 / Research</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="research-title">Questions worth<br>working through.</h2><p class="section-lead reading-copy">We study reality with the intention of expressing parts of it in machines. That requires understanding our models, their limits and ourselves.</p>
<dl class="research-themes"><div><dt><span>01</span>Intelligence &amp; learning</dt><dd>How do people and machines form models, learn from experience and use what they have learned in unfamiliar situations?</dd></div><div><dt><span>02</span>Novelty &amp; creativity</dt><dd>How does a new idea arise? What makes it useful? How could a machine explore possibilities and judge its own attempts?</dd></div><div><dt><span>03</span>Representing reality</dt><dd>What happens when we translate a concept, a physical process or a social practice into a definition, a model or code?</dd></div><div><dt><span>04</span>Human–machine ergonomics</dt><dd>How can people express intentions, inspect machine reasoning and intervene without carrying an ever-growing burden of supervision?</dd></div></dl>
</div></section>

<section id="lab" class="lab-section" aria-labelledby="lab-title"><div class="page-width section-grid">
<p class="section-marker">04 / Research into software</p>
<div class="section-content"><p class="eyebrow">CyberAlchemy Lab</p><h2 id="lab-title">An open-source<br>company brain system.</h2>
<div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">A company accumulates knowledge through people, projects, decisions and mistakes. Keeping that knowledge useful is a continuing task.</p><p>CyberAlchemy Lab organizes knowledge and work around explicit definitions, traceable evidence and declared rules for change. People and agents can recover what a project means, what supports its current state and what they may do next.</p></div>
<figure class="brain-overview"><div class="brain-context"><span>People</span><span>Projects</span><span>Agent sessions</span></div><div class="brain-state"><small>Durable project state</small><strong>Meaning. Evidence. Work. Decisions.</strong><span>Authority / Provenance / Lifecycle</span></div><figcaption>Agents work in temporary sessions. The project carries the continuing knowledge; each session receives a checked view of the context it needs.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="hero-actions"><a class="ds-button" href="start-here.html">Explore the Lab documentation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="company-brain.html">Why a company brain? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</div></div></section>

<section id="alignment" class="page-width research-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="alignment-title">
<p class="section-marker">05 / The longer horizon</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="alignment-title">Intelligence, with<br>direction and correction.</h2>
<div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">Our ambition reaches toward more general artificial intelligence. It begins with questions about human learning, intention, culture and judgment.</p><p>That ambition brings alignment into the same inquiry: how can AI behavior remain responsive to human intentions and values as systems become more capable? People disagree, situations change and a stated goal can leave important things unsaid. <a class="source-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.19852">Read the alignment survey</a>.</p>
<p>We investigate how intentions can be expressed, behavior examined and mistakes corrected. The Lab gives these questions a practical setting: explicit meanings, bounded permissions, evidence and accountable changes.</p><p>These structures help us formulate and examine alignment questions. Establishing that a machine behaves well requires evaluation, stress testing and oversight of its actual behavior. <a class="source-link" href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/team/alignment">Explore research on evaluation and oversight</a>.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="explore" class="page-width research-section section-grid explore-section" aria-labelledby="explore-title">
<p class="section-marker">06 / Explore the work</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="explore-title">Start with something<br>you can examine.</h2>
<div class="work-links"><a href="start-here.html"><span><small>Knowledge &amp; work</small><strong>CyberAlchemy Lab documentation</strong><span>Definitions, governance and the integrated model.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="../craft-documentation-proposal/craft-model.html#craft-overview"><span><small>Software design</small><strong>Craft</strong><span>Express software behavior in explicit models.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="../robot-learning-series/robot-learning-series.html"><span><small>Exploratory essays</small><strong>Learning through robot behavior</strong><span>Questions about experiments, physics and learning over time.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div>
<p class="closing-line">Bring a question. Follow its premises. See what survives examination.</p>
</div></section>
</main>
